+## Problem/Context
+Started the session mid-design with the prior session's 5 commits (seed type-math header + plan + async facade). This session pressure-tested and locked the design through a series of architectural questions. v5 sprawl: ~12.7K lines of per-lang extraction (rust/syn, ts/oxc, python/go/kotlin/tree-sitter) + scip + cst, with 3 kind reps, 4 span shapes, split identity (mint_sym/NodeIdx/WhereBytes), an eager engine, ~36GB RSS. The user wants max normalization WITHOUT false unification, rayon for CPU, sync core, reactivity elsewhere (RxJS prototype this iteration), a CLI that streams facts and races oxc, turnkey per-lang tests.
+
+## Solution/Approach (the locked design — canonical in _7_tasks.rs)
+The inversion stands: v5 mints coordinate strings inside the engine and writes rel tables; v6 emits span-addressed facts from a sync leaf and lets the store name them. This session's rulings:
+- D-families: families are TYPE-LEVEL. `Family` trait + marker structs (DfF/CallF/TypeF/ModuleF/CstF); `Node<F>`/`Edge<F>`; the `NodeKind`/`EdgeKind` SUMS DELETE. (Orthogonal axes aren't variants of one type; store splits by family anyway.) This killed the prefix-doubling smell the user flagged.
+- D-planes: 3 planes. RESOLUTION (Type|Call|Module, SCIP-wire, ratchet-able) + VALUE-FLOW (Df|Flow, native AST-only, the differentiator) + STRUCTURE (Cst, the lossless tree-sitter tree). Proved via a linear-independence argument that no family is a subset of another (Call needs cross-file resolution df lacks; Module is a family not a source; carries binding semantics SCIP/type flatten).
+- D-module: collapses. Resolution half -> SCIP namespace edges; binding half -> aux side metadata.
+- D-scip-wire: SCIP is a BIDIRECTIONAL wire (ScipOccurrence <-> Node<F>), not a one-way source. Our AST facts project OUT (joinable, ratchet-eligible); foreign indexers project IN. Round-trippable for the 3 resolution families ONLY (df/flow/cst/binding have no SCIP shape). Refines the user's "diet_scip" memory (v5 emitted facts in scip shape to join + ratchet best-producer).
+- D-ratchet: merge = per-fact best-producer-wins over N producers (Ast/Scip(&indexer)/Ghcacher). Producer tag rides the bundle, not the row. SCIP ground-truth for call/type/module is ONE rule, not the whole policy.
+- D-sync-only: the _6_facade async shell (ReactiveExtract/ProjectView) is CUT. Pure CPU + rayon; nothing awaits. Reactivity is the engine's (or the RxJS prototype's). SCIP build = std::process. (Supersedes the prior "sync core + async shell.")
+- D-adapter: the Node<F>->node_id / NameId->StrId / Span->file_bytes adapter lives ONCE in the main engine crate (doesn't exist yet; only sprefa-seed + sprefa-store exist).
+- D-port-clean, 3 langs: rust (syn), ts+js (oxc), go. python+kotlin deferred. Go has NO native Rust parser: Parser=tree-sitter, Project<F>/Resolve<F> walk the CST directly + scip-go. No buy-vs-buy gate.
+- D-concrete: concrete structs until a second impl.
+- identity: content-addressed, git-unbound. project = a corpus root (git worktree OR plain dir OR tarball); file = path + BlobHash; version (rev/now) is how bytes are FOUND, never the cache key. BlobSource is source-agnostic (GitShellout/Filesystem); git-fu (v5 repo.rs:1169 cat-file --batch, revid.rs) is ONE impl.
+- CPU trait factoring (one seam per dimension): Parser (syn/oxc/tree-sitter/ast-grep) / Project<F> (phase 1, content-keyed) / Resolve<F> (phase 2, project-keyed, reads ProjectCx) / Dispatch (ONE generic rayon orchestrator) / BlobSource / ScipSource. Closed vocabularies (kind enums, Producer, FamilyTag) stay enums; open extension points are traits.
+- CLI + streaming wire: a thin [[bin]] (clap + serde, NO tokio) wraps the sync lib, streams the FLAT tagged form (family, span, kind, name) as JSONL to stdout. Same flatten feeds the store seam + parity normalize (one flatten, three consumers). serde on the flat envelope, NOT on Node<F>. RxJS prototype drives it this iteration; the bin is also the purity-proof oracle vs biome/oxc.
+- turnkey tests: Tier-1 snapshot (one file + one fixture per lang; the codegen loop) + Tier-2 parity golden (v5-vs-v6 normalized diff; where v5's disparate inline tests unify behind the trait interface).
