+## Key Insights
+- Families are orthogonal axes, not variants: linear-independence proof (df is intra-procedural span-local; call is cross-file name-resolved; module is a family not a source and carries binding semantics; flow_edge is the diagonal joining df+call). Hence per-family types, never a sum.
+- CstF is a 5th family (the STRUCTURE plane): v5 cst.rs walk_cst enumerates the lossless named-node tree (node/child query rels, codemod anchors, spine). Coverage gap found in recon, closed. CstF kind is an OPEN interned grammar name (NameId), not a closed enum.
+- SCIP = bidirectional wire for the 3 RESOLUTION families only. df/flow/cst/binding have no SCIP shape and stay native. The ratchet governs the resolution plane; the "one query technique" goal is met by the in-memory _0_shape, not by forcing SCIP to carry value-flow.
+- The stdout JSONL wire = the store seam = the parity normalize: one flat tagged (family, span, kind, name) form, three consumers. serde on the flat envelope; Node<F> never crosses the seam or the stream.
+- ast-grep-as-Parser (not subprocess proxy) is what makes the piping proof abide the trait seams. ast-grep gives all 3 langs' grammars in one dep -> CstF piping proof lands for rust/ts/go at once.
+- "Don't leak the trait seams" = the wire is flat; Parser/Project<F>/Node<F> stay internal; the bin is the only public surface.
+- The user's banned-word + no-em-dash + dry style laws apply to docs too: both plan + ledger are at zero em dashes.
+- const_value: v5 brand [lit, template] (decls.rs:130); seed has 3 (+concat). Stays a Type-family aux. Reconcile variant count on port.
