+# Session: v6-sprefa-extract-ts-parity-gold-const-port
+
+## Goal
+Migrate v5's TS extraction fully into v6 (`sprefa-extract`) behind the uniform surface (`Source` / `Project<F>` / `ExtractOutput`), proven by a v5↔v6 parity golden. User-scoped this arc to **TS parity gold first**; rust (syn), go (tree-sitter+scip-go), and SCIP resolution (commit 4) are deferred follow-ons.
+
+## Current State
+Branch `plan/extract-golden-plan`. Three commits landed this session, all green (`cargo test` lib+bin+tests, `cargo tree` clean of tokio/sqlx/sea-orm/rusqlite/axum):
+- `78f919e8` **Epic U — the uniform surface**: `source.rs` (`Source` trait + `FamilyMask` + `ExtractOutput`) + `TsSource`/`AstgrepSource` behind a first-match `sources()`/`source_for()` roster. Collapsed 4 `dispatch_*` → one `dispatch(path,content,mask)`; 8 `flatten_*` → one `flatten`+`flatten_jsonl`; hand bin → `dispatch`+`flatten`+`--family`; 4 hand tests → one loop-driven `ts_uniform_surface` + roster test. `lang/oxc.rs` renamed `lang/ts.rs`.
+- `d192c63f` **Tier-2 parity gold (TS)**: `examples/v5_normalize.rs` (v5 in-process oracle) → committed `sample.v5.jsonl` → `tests/golden_parity.rs` twin-normalizes v6 `flatten` + diffs. Found + fixed ONE divergence: `CallKind::Free` tag `"free"`→`"function"` (v5 `call_def.kind`).
+- `eb4d8238` **const facet port (v5 model restored)**: `ConstWalker` (port of `ts_const_facts_from`) + `ConstValue`/`ConstKind` in `TypeFAux.consts` + `FlatFact::Const`. Added `consts.ts` fixture. Parity green: 5 Const entities + 11 const_value rows byte-match v5.
+
+## Problem/Context
+v5 extraction is a ~16.7K-line tangle (`mint_sym`, 3 span shapes, 3 kind reps, `NodeKind` sum) welded to sqlite; v6 rebuilds it as a normalized SYNC leaf (one byte `Span`, typed kinds, span-addressed identity, no DB). **v6 is a deliberately-isolated workspace** (its own `[workspace]`, "no v5 in the build graph") — so parity CANNOT be a live v5 link; it must be a **captured oracle**. v5's `TypeLang::extract/extract_calls/extract_dataflow` take just `(file, content)` → in-process, no DB, so the oracle is trivial to run. The const facet had been mis-framed as a false dichotomy ("consts stay df" → dropped the string-const entity v5 kept); user corrected: "do what 5 did."
+
+## Solution/Approach
+- **Uniform surface (Epic U)**: `Source` (name/matches/extract) is the `TypeLang` analog; `FamilyMask` gates families; `ExtractOutput` = one shared `Strings` + `Option<FamilyBundle<F>>` per family. Shared interner is byte-stable (flatten resolves NameId→&str at output). `TsSource::extract` = ast-grep for cst + ONE oxc parse feeding type/call/df.
+- **Captured-oracle parity**: `examples/v5_normalize.rs` (v5 root crate) runs `TsTypes.extract` in-process + emits canonical sorted tab-lines; committed as `<name>.v5.jsonl`; `golden_parity.rs` produces the SAME canonical lines from v6's `flatten` and asserts the PORTED set matches. **Coordinates**: df is byte-exact (v5 line+0-based-byte-col round-trips to v6 `Span.start`); type/call/const are line-exact (v5 drops byte offsets there, keeping only 1-based `line`). PORTED facets: type_node/type_sig/call_def/call_site/df_node/df_edge/const_value. DEFERRED v5-only: type_edge, df aux, docs. v6-only: cst (v5 has NO TS tree-sitter grammar → incomparable).
+- **Const port**: `ConstWalker` descends for string-bearing `const`/`as const` bindings → Const `Node<TypeF>` + `ConstValue` rows (lit cooked / template raw slice; object→dotted field paths; string-enum members key off enum entity). Driven from `TsSource::extract` (needs source bytes for template slices, which `Project::project` doesn't receive). v6 drops v5's scope/sym machinery (spans disambiguate).
+
