+## Key Insights
+- **Parity = captured oracle, never a live link** (v6 workspace deliberately isolated; v5 is the sqlite/tokio disease).
+- **Span lossiness**: v5 keeps byte offsets only for cst + df; type/call/const/doc are line-only. Parity is byte-exact for df, line-exact elsewhere.
+- **v5 has NO TS tree-sitter grammar** → CST parity impossible; v6 cst (ast-grep) is v6-only.
+- **CallKind::Free** tag must be `"function"` (v5), not `"free"` (v6 coinage) — for parity + wire compat.
+- **Const false dichotomy corrected**: a string const is a declaration (TypeF Const entity) AND a value (df `let_bind` node) AND carries its text (`const_value`) — all three, like v5; the df node is separate and unaffected.
+- `TypeLang::extract(file, content)` needs no DB/ProjectCx → in-process oracle is trivial.
+- v6 needs none of v5's `mint_sym`/scope machinery — spans disambiguate.
+- `Project::project` doesn't receive source bytes → any facet needing raw slices (template text) must run from `TsSource::extract`.
